          <attvalue for="3" value="en" />
          <attvalue for="4" value="PSA From CalOES Southern California Wildfire-Themed Scams Cyber criminals are currently exploiting the ongoing Southern California wildfires by using Southern California wildfire-themed lures for their phishing attempts and scams. Phishing is a type of social engineering attack that uses fraudulent messages to trick people into sharing sensitive information, such as account credentials or banking information. Phishing can be conducted through emails, text messages, QR codes, phone calls, and vo…" />
