          <attvalue for="4" value="@ai6yr In contrast, there were some really serious failures with the #EatonFire, starting with Edison's gross negligence starting it. Most of the people who died in West Altadena probably would have lived if the evacuation order hadn't been inexplicably delayed. Again, though, people literally saw the fire start, reported it immediately, and the fire department responded quickly. It's hard to believe it could have been stopped once it started." />
