      <node id="115368706009943775" label="@ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org: @camless Yep. USGS BAER does not work for SoCal. It's bad enough that…">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="109321601315889133" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="2025-10-13T20:19:02.000Z" />
          <attvalue for="3" value="en" />
          <attvalue for="4" value="@camless Yep. USGS BAER does not work for SoCal. It's bad enough that (for work) I built my own GIS layers for burn scar risk instead. Currently LA County and LA City are repeating the problem of Santa Barbara County before the Montecito mudflow, which is they are triggering the same evac zones for flood risk as wildfires. Santa Barbara fixed this, and they have zones specifically for flood risk (basically, the FEMA 100-year zone plus up into the watershed). But that's after so many people died…" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="context_descendants" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="2" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="5" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="11" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="3" />
          <attvalue for="13" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="2" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="115368737971181339" label="@camless@m.ai6yr.org: @ai6yr oh, interesting. I did something similar with our department o…">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="111270616296004000" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="camless@m.ai6yr.org" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="2025-10-13T20:27:11.000Z" />
          <attvalue for="3" value="en" />
          <attvalue for="4" value="@ai6yr oh, interesting. I did something similar with our department of geology for a fire that occurred in the Columbia Gorge earlier this year, The USGS model was really funky. The community is really concerned with the debris flow risk, partly due to previous debris flow event after the 2017 Eagle Creek Fire that caused a fatality. We need better models, but those that are being tested are still in the early development phases. I've been trying to put together a proposal for the legislature f…" />
          <attvalue for="5" value="" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="context_descendants" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="11" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="13" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="0" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="115369168978216318" label="@OLjohnel@m.ai6yr.org: @ai6yr @camless Those look like good starting points. Important to ad…">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="109371847891875579" />
          <attvalue for="1" value="OLjohnel@m.ai6yr.org" />
          <attvalue for="2" value="2025-10-13T22:16:47.000Z" />
          <attvalue for="3" value="en" />
          <attvalue for="4" value="@ai6yr @camless Those look like good starting points. Important to add alluvial fans because they aren't necessarily included in FEMA flood zones and by definition they show areas where streams deposit sediment (anything from mud and silt to boulders and trees)." />
          <attvalue for="5" value="" />
          <attvalue for="6" value="context_descendants" />
          <attvalue for="7" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="8" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="9" value="2" />
          <attvalue for="10" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="11" value="0" />
          <attvalue for="12" value="2" />
          <attvalue for="13" value="1" />
          <attvalue for="14" value="1" />
        </attvalues>
      </node>
      <node id="115369175615455880" label="@ai6yr@m.ai6yr.org: @OLjohnel @camless In LA County near Altadena, there's historical str…">
        <attvalues>
          <attvalue for="0" value="109321601315889133" />
